code_reads_beyond_parameters.cardlang:15:35: error: procedure 'f' reads the call-site pronoun 'actor'; a procedure body is spliced into call sites that need not share a call-site context — pass the value in as a parameter (`run f(actor)`)
code_reads_beyond_parameters.cardlang:15:35: error: procedure 'f' reads the call-site pronoun 'actor'; a procedure body is spliced into call sites that need not share a call-site context — pass the value in as a parameter (`run f(actor)`)
code_reads_beyond_parameters.cardlang:15:35: error: `actor` names the acting player, but it is read where no player is acting (outside any `as <player>`, `for each player`, `turns` or offered move, nobody is taking a turn), so it names no one. Name the player itself, or read it under a binder that names who acts (`as <player> { ... }`, `for each player p: ...`)
